# Local development: SQLite database
DATABASE_URL=file:/home/z/my-project/db/custom.db

# ============================================================
# Production (Vercel): PostgreSQL database
# ============================================================
# When deploying to Vercel, set DATABASE_URL in Vercel Environment Variables
# to a PostgreSQL connection string. The Prisma schema uses provider="postgresql".
#
# Recommended: Neon PostgreSQL (serverless-optimized, free tier available)
# https://neon.tech
#
# DATABASE_URL_PROD=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/tenetbid?schema=public
#
# For Neon with connection pooling (recommended for Vercel serverless):
# DATABASE_URL_PROD=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/tenetbid?schema=public&sslmode=require&connection_limit=5&pool_timeout=10
#
# Alternative: Vercel Postgres
# https://vercel.com/docs/storage/vercel-postgres
#
# DATABASE_URL_PROD=postgresql://default:xxxxx@ep-xxx.us-east-1.postgres.vercel-storage.com/verceldb?sslmode=require
#
# Alternative: Supabase
# https://supabase.com
#
# DATABASE_URL_PROD=postgresql://postgres.xxxx:xxxxx@aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=5&pool_timeout=10
#
# IMPORTANT: The db.ts module automatically appends connection_limit and pool_timeout
# in production when using a postgresql:// URL. You only need to set the base URL.
# ============================================================

# ============================================================
# File Storage: Vercel Blob (production) / Local filesystem (development)
# ============================================================
# In local development, uploaded files are stored in the /uploads/ directory
# and served via /api/uploads/ route with a Next.js rewrite from /uploads/*.
#
# In production (Vercel), files are stored in Vercel Blob.
# Set BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN in Vercel Environment Variables (dashboard).
# When this token is present, the storage module uses Vercel Blob;
# otherwise it falls back to local filesystem storage.
#
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=vercel_blob_rw_xxxxx_xxxxx  # Set in Vercel dashboard
# ============================================================
